"The prognosis is influenced by several factors, including a preoperative PSA of 7.93 and the pathological finding of positive surgical margins. The Gleason score was documented as 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2), which is favorable. A countervailing finding is that seminal vesicles were not invaded, and lymphovascular invasion was absent. Notably, no lymph nodes were removed, meaning nodal status assessment is incomplete, widening uncertainty in risk stratification. Biopsy-to-prostatectomy differences are noted as the biopsy Gleason pattern and ISUP report are missing. Prognostic revision would be significantly aided by postoperative PSA levels and tracking its subsequent trajectory over time. The current data suggests a need for caution due to positive margins and unknown nodal status. The fixed estimated horizon is 62.79 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 40.81–84.77 months; its coverage has not been validated."
